    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13683" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόσῑτ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσιτος</span>
			, <i>having eaten nothing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμερῶν τοσούτων ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					8.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.Byz.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				82.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hungry,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philonid.
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>having an aversion for food, without appetite,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.26
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σ́,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.635c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.654
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				6.190d
			</span></i>.</div>
